spoint 2026-06-07: player VRM looked up/down when the EDITOR fly-cam looked up/down (user report, confirmed fixed live). ROOT CAUSE: cam.yaw/cam.pitch are SHARED between the gameplay look and the editor fly-cam - camera.js editLook (right-button drag) mutates the same `pitch` field the gameplay look uses (camera.js:184 in the editMode update branch). app.js:351 copies them into input.yaw/input.pitch EVERY frame (else branch when not VR). The editor input-neutralization (app.js sendInput, the prior player-input-neutralized-in-editor fix) zeroed movement/shoot/aim/reload/interact but kept ...input INCLUDING yaw/pitch, so the editor fly-cam pitch flowed: sendInput.pitch -> server -> ps.lookPitch -> the local player animator setLookDirection (app.js:445, called even in the skipLocalRot editor branch) -> _lookPitch -> VRM head bone pitch. FIX (commit on main): module vars _frozenLookYaw/_frozenLookPitch captured each NON-editing frame; while editing, the sendInput override pins yaw:_frozenLookYaw,pitch:_frozenLookPitch so the avatar holds its pre-edit gaze and the fly-cam roams independently; on exit the override stops so live look resumes immediately. NO animator-side change needed - with the sent pitch frozen, ps.lookPitch converges to the frozen value and setLookDirection correctly HOLDS the pre-edit gaze (forcing 0 would wrongly snap the head level). Browser-witnessed (session 23): editLook pitched cam to -1.4 but sentInEditorPitches [0,0,0] frozen, ps.lookPitch 0.209 does NOT track fly-cam -0.787, exit restores. XSTATE AUDIT (per request): locoMachine (AnimationStateMachine.js:44) transitions complete (every state->IdleLoop, Death->REVIVE, sprint-stick LOCO_COOLDOWN already guarded by sendLoco/LOCO_EVENT_TARGET); in editor movement is zeroed so it rests in IdleLoop. clientMachine editor mode resets gizmo+select on enter/exit; all freeze consumers gate on isEditor. editor-assert.js gained a no-look-pitch-in-editor assertion. EXTENDS [[editor-interactions-pick-hookflow-shoot-fixes]]; the shared cam.pitch field is the gotcha - freezing must happen at the input-send boundary, not the camera (the fly-cam legitimately needs that pitch).